@*
    The consuming site's layout — deliberately somebody else's, because that is what uBookIt
    always sits inside. It carries its own font, colours and chrome, and uBookIt inherits all
    of them: the package sets no text colour of its own, so every colour here resolves through
    `currentColor` or `inherit`.

    The one uBookIt-specific line is the _Styles partial, exactly as docs/booking-page.md tells
    a site author to add it. Use the partial rather than a hand-written <link>: a theme turns
    the partial off and would not turn a hand-written link off.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@(ViewData["Title"] ?? "Fairfield Studios")</title>
    <style>
        :root { color-scheme: light dark; }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.5;
            color: #1c2024;
            background: #fff;
        }

        header {
            border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e5e8;
            padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
            display: flex;
            align-items: baseline;
            gap: 1.5rem;
        }

        header strong { font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
        header nav { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        header nav a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
        header nav a[aria-current="page"] { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }

        main { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; }

        footer {
            border-top: 1px solid #e3e5e8;
            padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: #5b6169;
        }

        @@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body { color: #e7e9ea; background: #16181a; }
            header, footer { border-color: #2b2f33; }
            footer { color: #9ba1a8; }
        }
    </style>

    @* uBookIt's stylesheet. One line, and it is the line the docs ask for. *@
    @await Html.PartialAsync("~/Views/Shared/UBookIt/_Styles.cshtml")
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <strong>Fairfield Studios</strong>
        <nav>
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <a href="/book/" aria-current="page">Book</a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
        @RenderBody()
    </main>

    <footer>
        A development harness for uBookIt. Not a real business.
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
